{"name":"Clayton","hex":"#83756c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Clayton","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A placename:\nA large number of places in the United States:\nA town, the county seat of Barbour County, Alabama; named for Georgia jurist and congressman Augustin Smith Clayton.\nA city in Contra Costa County, California; named for founder Joel Henry Clayton.","A large number of places in the United States:\nA town, the county seat of Barbour County, Alabama; named for Georgia jurist and congressman Augustin Smith Clayton.\nA city in Contra Costa County, California; named for founder Joel Henry Clayton."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Clayton"}],"entries":[{"title":"Clayton (name)","blocks":[{"text":"Clayton is both an English surname and a masculine given name. Notable people with the name include:"}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clayton_(name)"},{"title":"Clayton baronets","blocks":[{"text":"There have been three baronetcies created for persons named Clayton, two in the Baronetage of Great Britain and one in the Baronetage of the United Kingdom. One creation is extant as of 2026."},{"items":["Clayton baronets of Marden Park (1732), later Clayton-East baronets and Clayton-East-Clayton baronets","Clayton baronets of Adlington (1774)","Clayton-East baronets of Hall Place (1838), later Gilbert-East baronets and Clayton-East-Clayton baronets"]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clayton_baronets"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"Clayton":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/03/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-Clayton.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/0/03/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-Clayton.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-Clayton.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transc